{
  "_note": "Sols past the first (design/story.md section 4, Chapter 1), in data/beats.json's beat schema (its _note). A key per sol: beats.start_sol(sol) plays it when the kid wakes on that sol (after cine's night sleep, the rules' sim.sol). Feel first, then PIP names it, once. Mission 1 is keys 2 to 10 (design/plans/mission-1.md, mission-1-contracts.md): a teaching line shows for its `wait.time` and never stops the game, its `page` lands in the handbook, and each sol asks one `check` after its last lesson; Mission 2 (key 13 on) still has facts that wait for a dismiss. Sol 2: one wing brushed, then the kid goes to the reactor (about 190 m out) on foot or in the rover (the body rides on the seat, so the place counts while driving): the step ends within 4.5 m of the reactor item's middle ([-154.457, -112.219], world.json; its frame is 4 m across, so 2.5 m from its pads), not near the landmark reactor, a viewpoint 21 m short of it, which once ended it from 35 m (15 Nov playtest); the waypoint is on the item (sandbox.gd _point); brushing more wings first is the kid's own trade. The toxic_dust page (rows 140, 142) lands the first time PIP says the suit is dusty (sandbox.gd, advisor.say), not at Sol 2's dust lesson, which never says it: the advisor's `need.dusty` sends the kid to the brush from then on. Sol 4: the alarm's beat starts the rules' oxygen leak (`do: event:o2_leak`, beats.rule; the valve's use ends it) and shows no waypoint, the handbook's oxygen_valve page says where; its `nag` reminders say it too. The game ends after Sol 10 (beats.LAST_SOL, 15 Nov): next_sol() never leads past it, and Sol 10's sleep shows the Mission 1 report (the root's _rule report:mission1, hud.show_report) and then the end screen (sandbox.gd end_screen()); keys 13 on stay for Missions 2 and 3 and are reached only by a test or the debug jump. Sol 5: the Shift lesson on the way to the shelter; the card sol5_storm applies nothing, the kid's own place does (the root halves the dose while the hero stands in the shelter, and wings brushed in free play give the power). Key 6: the M lesson when the trip is planned. Each sol's work ends with day_done: PIP leads to HAB 1's airlock and the Today list keeps only the rest (beats.REST), and the bed opens only then (beats.may_sleep; not on Sol 5, where PIP stays in the shelter). Then free play: everything allowed, PIP let go (pip.release), the Today list says sleep and points at HAB 1, until the next night's sleep (event slept). Every number PIP says has a factcheck row, named per beat in `fact_rows`. Spots: [27.95, 9.5] is wing1's clean_panel stand, [28.5, 7] open ground south of it, short of the wing rows; [-11, 0.5] just inside the greenhouse's door. pip.place: put PIP at a spot before its order (unseen, the night has passed: a sol may end with PIP far from the base). Sol 2's dust comes from the rules: data/sim.json schedule fires dust_gust at Sol 2, 03:00, overnight. Sol 4: `do: mail` sends the visor mail (beats.send_mail, the HUD's send_mail), and the reply comes back as mail_arrived (the HUD's mail cue); `wait.ever` counts an event that came before its beat, since the valve may take longer than the 22 minute round trip. Sol 5: to_shelter ends 0.6 m from the shelter's middle, where the whole body is inside its room (player.room). Sol 5: the rules' schedule starts the ARCHIVED X12 flare at 07:00 (data/sim.json), the wiring tells the beats event:<id>, and being in the storm shelter's room sets the rules' sheltered knob (half the dose). Sol 6: the quiet sols 6 to 8 are slept through at once (`do: skip:3`, beats.skip_sols: the rules' skip_sols, then the HUD's ledger card); its close comes back as ledger_closed, and the day goes on as Sol 9. The skip lands on Sol 9's morning, so key 6 goes on with Sol 9 'First field trip': plan on the map, board the rover, `do: trip:<landmark>` (beats.trip, cine.trip_to, answered with arrived:<landmark>) to the Mont Mercou site, a sample, and the trip home Sol 10, Mission 1's finale 'The sky goes dark': no skip, the kid wakes into the dust storm (the rules' storm starts in Sol 9's night, data/sim.json schedule; the old beat ids s12_* stay). The wake's `do` turns the look: clock:storm jumps it to the storm at noon, clock:6.5 puts it back at the rules' wake hour (sim.json wake_hour) and clock:run lets it run, so the sky is dark at the rules' hour when the kid steps out. Out to PIP, the dark sky felt first, then named: the wings, the reactor, storms that cover all of Mars; one check; the storm power choice (beats.json offers sol12_power); Mission 1's last line (m1_done); the walk home. The sleep after it lands on Sol 11, and the game ends there. Sol 13: a dusty suit brushed off in HAB 1 (use brush), then the stormy sols 13 to 16 skipped (`skip:4`), and key 13 goes on as Sol 17: the first salad from the greenhouse (use harvest). The 2018 storm's sky clears with a 43 sol e-fold (row 182), so the storm look and the rules' dim sun stay on past Sol 17: no 'clear sky' line Sol 18: the stormy sols 18 and 19 skipped (`skip:2`), and key 18 goes on as Sol 20 'The long drive' to Curiosity's sol 5070 spot (site_curiosity, 14.3 km, outside the walk-home ring): look, never touch, the trip home (the overnight in the rover and Sol 22's low battery are not played). Sol 21: the calm sols 21 to 25 skipped (`skip:5`), Sol 26: the sample case lifted and carried to the rocket (item mav) and set down, sols 26 to 30 skipped, and on Sol 31 `do: liftoff` (beats.liftoff, cine.launch, answered with launched); PIP's last lines are the result. A skip later in a sequence waits on the `event` ledger_closed, not `ever`: `ever` counts the wake's own ledger",
  "deadline": {
    "_note": "A sol's tasks belong to that sol (skills/guided-tutorial row 6): while they are not done, PIP warns at these local hours of the day it began (art direction; the sun sets about 17:50), and once more at the rules' hold before the next wake (sim.awake_left). A late night has its cost in the rules: a night's sleep is never shorter than sleep_h (data/sim.json), so a kid who stays up wakes late",
    "warn": [[16.0, "deadline.sunset"], [18.5, "deadline.night"], [22.0, "deadline.late"]],
    "dawn": "deadline.dawn"
  },
